- `action(n1, "start review process")`: Hallucinates an introductory task not documented in the source, which explicitly states the clerk should "start by reviewing the received application".
- `action(n12, "end")`: Hallucinates a terminal action step; the description simply states "the process will come to an end", which is correctly captured by `end(e1)` without an intervening action.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Violates actor fidelity (SMC7); the source assigns all responsibilities to "the review clerk", but the model declares the participant as "Default".